# Level checkpoints are large (16-42 MB each) and hold latents, not pictures.
*.pt
*.pt.tmp

# decoded*/ IS TRACKED, deliberately. The earlier rule ignored it as "regenerable", which is false in
# this repo's own terms: decode_levels.py regenerates the PNGs from levels_*.pt / partial_*.pt, and
# those are ignored by the rule above -- so the images only survive as long as the checkpoints sit on
# $WORK. The summary grid is not a substitute either: strong_tilt_grid_*.png is 2500x1416 for 8x16
# tiles, ~156x177 per particle, against 512x512 for the real thing.
# COST: ~0.44 MB per PNG, ~50 MB per leg, permanent (PNGs do not delta-compress). Budget for that
# before adding a leg, or decode a subset of levels.
